{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/152829-a-product-i-would-like-to-see","id":152829,"title":"A Product I would Like To See","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-05-29T12:49:42-07:00","id":152829,"title":"A Product I would Like To See","content":"Thinking about how I run Scion there's a product I'd like to see.<br /> <br /> I run Scion as the myth and magic coming back into the world and it NOT being particularly secret. Scions may individually want to keep a low profile but more than a few will happily let the spotlight fall on them.<br /> <br /> To that end what usually happens is that the media latches on to the weirdness and starts reporting it, regular people flock to Twitter and Facebook and 4chan and so on. Over time the Scions become media focal points, some try to hide from it and others revel in it, battles down Oxford street with Jotun and other Titanspawn and a handful of Scions in gleaming gold and Relic weaponry while a crowd panics, flees and watches, smartphones out. Ancient zuggurats rise and regenrate and get in the news with monsters flooding from them, etc.<br /> <br /> Scion alongside a media frenzy from celebrity culture magazines to political pundits and Scions running for office and being moral guides etc.<br /> <br /> So. I'd love to see a book or PDF or similar product that looks at the actions of Scions through the lens of celebrity magazines, media talking heads, facebook comment threads, forum chatter, anti-Scion human rights groups rallies, religious argument and debate etc.<br /> <br /> Basically a book from the 'outside looking in' how the majority of normal people will experience the returns of myth and magic into the world, namely, through the media.<br /> <br /> With nice stylized art mimicking glossy gossip magazines ('Love handles, does Aphrodite like them? We talk to Johnny Rhodes exclusively on page 4!), pages styled to look like a forum thread ('Who would win, Eric Donner vs. Bruce Lee'), silly meme photos from the bowels of 4chan ('Sucellus' hammer, 20% cooler than Mjolnir!') and so on.<br /> <br /> Am I alone in my desire to see media sensationalised Scion?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-29T12:55:34-07:00","id":152864,"title":"","content":"I think this is a very neat idea. It's kind of like a new angle on fatebonds and such. Interesting!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2775-varygoode","name":"varygoode","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-29T13:34:13-07:00","id":152900,"title":"","content":"Huh. Sounds interesting; an Aberrant-style look at Scion.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/3533-scion-general-questions?p=20495#post20495\">It sounds like whether or not there's a Masquerade</a> is set to change in 2e's settings, so we might see settings where they are that public, and others where they're quieter. Be a good premise for a PDF where they _are_ that public.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-29T16:33:09-07:00","id":153225,"title":"","content":"I'm personally a fan of Masquerade Scion, because I like to run people's reactions to things in as realistic a way as I am able, and I think that the realistic actions of nation-states upon the discovery of metahumans would be capture to study, and if that fails, destroy with overwhelming force. I just don't think most people would be comfortable with literal deities running around, to say nothing for the implications to the world's primarily-monotheist religions (though the hindus would get a big ol' &quot;told you so&quot; moment). And because IMHO large groups of forewarned, well-armed, well-trained humans can easily be threats to low-Legend Scions, I doubt that Scions who broke masquerade too hard would necessarily survive to the power level where humans were no longer a threat (I generally consider the threshold to be Legend 4)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Games are a way for us to explore what it means to be human, or inhuman, as the case may be. Let's all have a good time playing them.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/400-guitarsniper","name":"guitarsniper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-29T17:00:20-07:00","id":153246,"title":"","content":"Hmm...The big three religions will love this idea....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-30T02:50:06-07:00","id":153630,"title":"","content":"A world with scions in the media would certainly be more realistic, having a book go over details of such would take a load of work off the home GM. Masquerades are a lot less sensible now than they were 10 years ago. We have cameras EVERYWHERE, there's no way to elude them unless you literally stay away from populated areas, so of course this kind of thing would crop up in the media. A low level or non-com scion woudl definitely have to keep their head down in our world, yes, but that's because a humanoid titanspawn is perfectly capable of buying smartphones, cameras, computers, and internet access. They could use all this modern madness to easily track a newbie scion down.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-31T19:31:43-07:00","id":155375,"title":"","content":"It's sort of hard to justify a totally 'open' world where the myths are walking down Park Ave with a ticker tape parade. And parts of Scion very strongly hint that creatures have a bit of the Mist (from Percy Jackson) unless it's brought to the attention of the mortal.<br /> <br /> Like a fire giant just looks like a big, burnt dude and not a giant with flaming hair.<br /> <br /> I think they might actually be increasing that sort of 'veil' between mortal and immortal lives.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1246-arthurhansen","name":"ArthurHansen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1246_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-01T00:37:26-07:00","id":155536,"title":"","content":"One of the big positives for my players was being able to let loose and do the crazy stuff in full view of people and not have some overbearing V:tM style Masquerade-police coming down on them. One of the best sessions I ran had them on a plane flying to Morocco that was attacked by a Nemean Vulture and a swarm of Harpies. There was a dynamic gunfight down the aisle, epic sword duel atop the wings and acrobatic mayhem atop the fuselage while the fourth guy landed the plane safely on the runway. Hundreds of passengers saw it all (though many died...) and the landing on the runway was observed by media and emergency services and public in general.<br /> <br /> So, not necessarily a tickertape parade waiting for them to <i>start</i> with. More panic and confusion. But after a while (assuming the Scions don't go crazy) you could end up in the media as guest columnists...especially considering the Epic Charisma and Manipulation types out there.<br /> <br /> So if you were going to do the book perhaps have the earlier pages (with date stamps) as panicked news articles and confused speculation on twitter feeds and forums and by the end of the book (with much later date stamps) having tentative interviews with the more sociable Scions and have flyers for anti-Scion rallies using images of the less wholesome looking Scions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-01T01:44:35-07:00","id":155555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArthurHansen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/152829-a-product-i-would-like-to-see?p=155375#post155375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's sort of hard to justify a totally 'open' world where the myths are walking down Park Ave with a ticker tape parade. And parts of Scion very strongly hint that creatures have a bit of the Mist (from Percy Jackson) unless it's brought to the attention of the mortal.<br /> <br /> Like a fire giant just looks like a big, burnt dude and not a giant with flaming hair.<br /> <br /> I think they might actually be increasing that sort of 'veil' between mortal and immortal lives.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It is actually started off as &quot;People see a large dude with a sunburn and red hair&quot; type of stuff, but it is because the Mythic has been hidden for so long that people don't realize what they're looking at, it's sort of a think like when Werewolves let themselves be seen in WoD, but without the fear. People rationalize what it is that they see, their minds having been closed to the possibility of the supernatural. But once things start happening, they start seeing scions fight and whatnot people will become more aware and eventually perception will shift so that the world will see the world for what it is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'll be your Huckleberry","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2397-the-dude","name":"The Dude","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-01T04:13:12-07:00","id":155588,"title":"","content":"Hm. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/258-scion-origin-whats-the-deal?p=49854#post49854\">A possibly relevant comment from Joe</a>:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Inspired by stories as myriad as Butcher's Dresden to the works of Charles de Lint and everything inbetween (and beyond), we'd like this game to provide some inspiration for the sorts of stories you might tell about a world that has seen an upswing in Legend once more and how that affects normal folks. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-01T06:40:37-07:00","id":155611,"title":"","content":"It's fun to imagine it, but if a &quot;real case scenario&quot; is desired in some way, I would think a lot of culturally relevant folks would either be dismayed at their gods showing up, or relieved and return to actively worship them. (This could be positive or negative. E.g. &quot;Asatru&quot; is cool for evolved Norse beliefs, but the old &quot;blood eagle&quot; would probably be frowned upon in many countries)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-01T08:59:38-07:00","id":155679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/152829-a-product-i-would-like-to-see?p=155611#post155611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's fun to imagine it, but if a &quot;real case scenario&quot; is desired in some way, I would think a lot of culturally relevant folks would either be dismayed at their gods showing up, or relieved and return to actively worship them. (This could be positive or negative. E.g. &quot;Asatru&quot; is cool for evolved Norse beliefs, but the old &quot;blood eagle&quot; would probably be frowned upon in many countries)</div> </div> </div> </div>I think a key point though would be that the Scions of those old gods would have been raised with a modern mindset. So, sure, ritual sacrifice and the like may be something the gods want to see again but the Scions representing them may well push back and drive some cultural change within those older traditions. Sounds like some interesting space for intergenerational conflict between the Gods and their Scions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}